            {
              "id": "a6928deb-7ece-3817-b08c-7daa4d7c3917",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Shell Process Initiation: Potential Injection Vulnerability Detected\" vulnerability in Python refers to the potential for an attacker to inject malicious code into the system command being executed by the Python script. This is possible when user input or other untrusted data is used to construct a system command without proper sanitization or validation. In the provided code example, the `os.system()` function is used to execute a system command that includes the results of `test_bin(\"onmetis\")` and `graph`, which could potentially be manipulated to include malicious commands.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, avoid using `os.system()` or similar functions that execute shell commands with user-provided or untrusted input. If it's necessary to use such functions, ensure that the input is properly sanitized and validated to prevent command injection. \n\nConsider using safer alternatives that don't involve shell command execution, such as the `subprocess` module's functions, which are designed to replace the `os.system()` function. These functions don't spawn a shell by default, making them less vulnerable to shell injection attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere's a safer version of the code using `subprocess.run()`:\n\n```python\nimport subprocess\n\nsubprocess.run([test_bin(\"onmetis\"), graph])\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following Python standard library:\n\n- `os` or `subprocess`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Command Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n- [CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "B605",
                  "a6928deb-7ece-3817-b08c-7daa4d7c3917"
                ]
              }
            },
