            {
              "id": "21ca413c-c35c-3209-9a5e-281a3ccbcb48",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Shell Process Initiation: Potential Injection Vulnerability Detected\" vulnerability in Python refers to the potential for an attacker to inject malicious code into the system command that is being executed. This is possible when user input is used to construct a system command without proper sanitization or validation. In the provided code example, the `os.system()` function is used to execute a system command that includes user input, which could potentially be manipulated by an attacker.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to avoid using the `os.system()` function to execute system commands that include user input. Instead, use safer alternatives such as the `subprocess` module which can handle arguments as a list, reducing the risk of shell injection vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the provided code example:\n\n```python\nimport subprocess\n\nsubprocess.run([test_bin(\"pmetis\"), graph, '2'])\n```\n\nIn this revised code, the `subprocess.run()` function is used instead of `os.system()`. The arguments are passed as a list, which prevents shell injection attacks.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following Python libraries:\n\n- `os` (built-in)\n- `subprocess` (built-in)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Command Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n- [CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "B605",
                  "21ca413c-c35c-3209-9a5e-281a3ccbcb48"
                ]
              }
            },
