            {
              "id": "e15c16fa-b432-3c81-be67-2fbceec834a3",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nIn Python, the `chmod` function is used to change the permissions of a file or a directory. The `chmod(file, 0o755)` function sets the permissions of the file to `755` in octal, which means read, write, and execute permissions for the owner, and read and execute permissions for the group and others.\n\nThis can lead to a file permission vulnerability if sensitive data is stored in the file, as it allows anyone on the system to read and execute the file. This could potentially lead to unauthorized access or information disclosure.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should:\n\n- Limit the permissions of the file to only what is necessary. For example, if the file does not need to be executed, do not give it execute permissions.\n- Do not give read or execute permissions to the group or others if they do not need it.\n- Consider using access control lists (ACLs) for more granular control over file permissions.\n- Regularly review and audit file permissions to ensure they are set correctly.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of `chmod(file, 0o755)`, consider using `chmod(file, 0o700)` if only the owner needs to read, write, and execute the file. This will prevent the group and others from accessing the file.\n\n```python\nimport os\n\n# Incorrect: Gives read, write, and execute permissions to the owner, and read and execute permissions to the group and others\nos.chmod(file, 0o755)\n\n# Correct: Gives read, write, and execute permissions to the owner only\nos.chmod(file, 0o700)\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe `os` module is part of the Python Standard Library, so no additional library dependencies are required.\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-732: Incorrect Permission Assignment for Critical Resource](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "B103"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "0d1aa755-1672-3ce8-a388-061723c03805",
              "name": "resources.rules.dangerous-system-call",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Opengrep Finding: resources.rules.dangerous-system-call"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
