            {
              "id": "57edea90-e127-3902-92ec-6efd149bad21",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring()` function in Python's standard library is vulnerable to XML External Entity (XXE) attacks. This vulnerability can be exploited when parsing untrusted XML data. An attacker can use this vulnerability to disclose internal files using the file URI handler, cause denial of service, and launch other types of attacks.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using `xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring()` to parse untrusted XML data. Instead, use the equivalent function from the `defusedxml` library, which is designed to mitigate XXE attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace:\n\n```python\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\ntree = ET.fromstring(document)\n```\n\nWith:\n\n```python\nfrom defusedxml import ElementTree as ET\ntree = ET.fromstring(document)\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe `defusedxml` library is required by the fixed code example. You can install it using pip:\n\n```bash\npip install defusedxml\n```\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XXE Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/XML_External_Entity_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference ('XXE')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "B314",
                  "57edea90-e127-3902-92ec-6efd149bad21"
                ]
              }
            },
