            {
              "id": "93b04c24-0962-3c80-ae42-84e89d4af2b7",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe MD5 hash function is considered weak due to its vulnerability to collision attacks. This means that two different inputs can produce the same hash output, which can lead to security issues. In Python, the `hashlib.md5()` function has a `usedforsecurity` parameter that defaults to `True`. If this parameter is set to `False`, it indicates that the hash function is not being used for a security-sensitive operation, and thus the weak MD5 hash function can be used without raising a warning.\n\nHowever, if the MD5 hash function is used in a security-sensitive context with `usedforsecurity=False`, it can lead to vulnerabilities. An attacker could exploit this to generate a different input that produces the same MD5 hash as the expected input, leading to unauthorized access or other security breaches.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nAvoid using the MD5 hash function for security-sensitive operations. Instead, use a stronger hash function such as SHA-256. If you must use MD5, ensure that the `usedforsecurity` parameter is set to `True` to raise a warning if a weak hash function is used.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the MD5 hash function with a stronger hash function. Here's how you can do it with SHA-256:\n\n```python\nimport hashlib\n\nloaded_checksum = hashlib.sha256(packagebody).hexdigest()\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `hashlib` library, which is included in the Python Standard Library.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Insecure Cryptographic Storage](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A3_2017-Sensitive_Data_Exposure)\n- [CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "B324",
                  "93b04c24-0962-3c80-ae42-84e89d4af2b7"
                ]
              }
            },
