            {
              "id": "aeb82de2-54e3-315d-88cd-28c54d0dda2d",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Vulnerability in URL Audit for Permitted Schemes\" is a security vulnerability in Python programming language that occurs when a URL is not properly validated before being used to perform network operations. This can lead to various security issues such as remote file inclusion (RFI), local file inclusion (LFI), and server-side request forgery (SSRF). In the provided code snippet, the `urlopen` function from the `urllib.request` module is used to open a URL without any validation, which can lead to these security issues.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to validate the URL before using it to perform network operations. This can be done by checking the scheme of the URL and ensuring that it is one of the permitted schemes (e.g., http or https). Additionally, it is also recommended to use a safe library or function that performs this validation automatically.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a fixed version of the provided code snippet:\n\n```python\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\nimport urllib.request\n\ndef safe_urlopen(url):\n    parsed_url = urlparse(url)\n    if parsed_url.scheme not in ['http', 'https']:\n        raise ValueError(f'Invalid scheme: {parsed_url.scheme}')\n    return urllib.request.urlopen(url)\n\npackagebody = safe_urlopen(url).read()\n```\n\nIn this fixed version, the `urlparse` function from the `urllib.parse` module is used to parse the URL and check its scheme before opening it with `urlopen`.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- urllib\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-918: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/918.html)\n- [CWE-23: Relative Path Traversal](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/23.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "B310",
                  "aeb82de2-54e3-315d-88cd-28c54d0dda2d"
                ]
              }
            },
